menu "BLE WiFi Provisioning Configuration"

config BLE_PROV_NV_ENABLE
    bool "Enable NV storage for WiFi credentials"
    default y
    help
        When enabled, WiFi SSID and password are saved to NV (non-volatile)
        storage after a successful provisioning. On the next boot the device
        will skip BLE advertising and connect directly.

config BLE_PROV_AUTO_RECONNECT
    bool "Auto reconnect on boot if configured"
    depends on BLE_PROV_NV_ENABLE
    default y
    help
        If NV credentials exist at boot, skip BLE provisioning entirely
        and reconnect to the saved WiFi network automatically.

config BLE_PROV_LED_ENABLE
    bool "Enable LED status indication"
    default n
    help
        Drive a GPIO-connected LED to show provisioning state visually.
        States: fast blink (BLE advertising), slow blink (WiFi connecting),
        solid on (success), 3 fast blinks then off (failure/timeout).

config BLE_PROV_LED_PIN
    int "LED GPIO pin number"
    depends on BLE_PROV_LED_ENABLE
    default 7
    help
        GPIO pin connected to the status LED (active-high).
        Default 7 is the HiHope WS63E EVB red LED.

config BLE_PROV_TIMEOUT_SEC
    int "Provisioning timeout (seconds)"
    default 60
    range 10 300
    help
        If no phone connects via BLE within this timeout, provisioning
        stops and the device enters a low-power idle state.

config BLE_PROV_MAX_RETRIES
    int "Maximum provisioning retries"
    default 3
    range 1 10
    help
        Number of times the device will retry WiFi connection before
        giving up and entering deep idle.

config BLE_PROV_BTN_ENABLE
    bool "Enable button to clear NV credentials (long-press)"
    depends on BLE_PROV_NV_ENABLE
    default n
    help
        When enabled, a long press (~3 seconds) on the configured GPIO
        pin clears saved WiFi credentials from NV and reboots the device,
        allowing re-provisioning.  Button is active-low with internal pull-up.

config BLE_PROV_BTN_PIN
    int "Button GPIO pin number"
    depends on BLE_PROV_BTN_ENABLE
    default 13
    help
        GPIO pin for the clear-credentials button (active-low).
        Connect button between this pin and GND.

endmenu
